{
  "id": "20817_wananikakeru",
  "headword": "{罠|わな}にかける",
  "reading": "わなにかける",
  "part_of_speech": "expression, verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to trap; to ensnare; to set someone up",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to trap; to ensnare (literally)",
      "explanation": "To catch an animal or person using a trap or snare."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to set someone up; to trick into a trap",
      "explanation": "To deceive or manipulate someone into a disadvantageous situation through cunning or deception."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20817_wananikakeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{熊|くま}を{罠|わな}にかけた。",
      "english": "They trapped a bear.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20817_wananikakeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{猟師|りょうし}が{罠|わな}にかけた{鹿|しか}を{回収|かいしゅう}した。",
      "english": "The hunter retrieved the deer he had trapped.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20817_wananikakeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{野生動物|やせいどうぶつ}を{罠|わな}にかけるには{経験|けいけん}と{忍耐|にんたい}が{必要|ひつよう}だ。",
      "english": "Trapping wild animals requires experience and patience.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20817_wananikakeru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{罠|わな}にかけられた。",
      "english": "He was set up.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20817_wananikakeru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{敵|てき}を{罠|わな}にかける{作戦|さくせん}を{立|た}てた。",
      "english": "They devised a plan to trap the enemy.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20817_wananikakeru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{巧妙|こうみょう}な{手口|てぐち}で{詐欺師|さぎし}が{被害者|ひがいしゃ}を{罠|わな}にかけた。",
      "english": "The scammer trapped the victim with a clever scheme.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "An expression combining {罠|わな} (trap/snare) with かける (to set/apply). Used both literally for animal trapping and figuratively for deceiving or setting people up.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {罠|わな}にはまる: to fall into a trap\n- {罠|わな}を{仕掛|しか}ける: to set a trap\n- {罠|わな}から{逃|のが}れる: to escape from a trap\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {騙|だま}す: to deceive — more general deception\n- {陥|おとしい}れる: to entrap — more formal, implies causing someone's downfall\n- はめる: to frame — colloquial, to set someone up",
